<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!-- Landscape counterpart to values/dimens.xml's status_bar_height_landscape.

         AOSP keeps these two in lockstep and this tree had only moved one of
         them. values-land/dimens.xml:33 defines quick_qs_offset_height as a
         reference to @dimen/status_bar_height_landscape, so it follows the
         override to 25dp automatically. quick_qs_total_height at :34-35 is a
         LITERAL 152dp, with AOSP's own comment saying it is "effectively
         status_bar_height_landscape + 128" - i.e. 24 + 128, computed against the
         AOSP value, not against ours.

         AOSP's own cutout overlays do the same arithmetic by hand and prove the
         rule: packages/overlays/DisplayCutoutEmulationTallOverlay/res/values-land/
         config.xml:19-21 pairs 28dp with 156dp.

         25 + 128 = 153. Consumers are SystemUI's
         res/layout/quick_status_bar_expanded_header.xml:23,
         QuickStatusBarHeader.java:444 and StatusBar.java:3006. Left at 152 the
         quick-settings header is one dp short of its own offset in landscape.

         Portrait needs no equivalent: values/dimens.xml's 48dp offset already
         clears the 45dp status bar, and 176 = 48 + 128 is consistent. -->
    <dimen name="quick_qs_total_height">153dp</dimen>
</resources>
